regime switch is present**, centered at t \u2248 71322.\n\n**Coordinated cohort replacement.** Comparing the 5000-unit half-windows [66323, 71322] vs [71323, 76322], every group member tested switched to a **completely disjoint** contact set (Jaccard = 0 in all six cases, step_32):\n\n| Node | Before (old cohort) | After (new cohort) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 59 | 58, 247, 383, 959, 1071, 1136, 1283, 1291, 1713, 1761 | 393, 402, 861, 928, 1014, 1032, 1605 |\n| 881 | 383, 424, 721, 794, 1071, 1136, 1713, 1757 | 184, 393, 402, 686, 879, 928, 1014, 1032 |\n| 325 | 58, 247, 424, 429, 1136, 1283 | 138, 402, 613, 686, 861, 879, 928, 970, 1032, 1605 |\n| 1034 | 58, 247, 383, 429, 870, 959, 1071, 1136, 1283, 1291, 1713, 1761 | 402, 613, 686, 861, 879, 895, 928, 1032, 1605, 1999 |\n| 617 | 58, 247, 383, 424, 429, 959, 1071, 1136, 1283, 1761 | 138, 402, 686, 879, 944, 970, 1014, 1032, 1605 |\n| 743 | 383, 429, 721, 794, 959, 1291, 1713, 1757, 1761 | 393, 861, 879, 895, 944, 970, 1032, 1605, 1999 |\n\n**Abruptness, not drift.** The old cohort collapses rather than fading: nodes 58, 247, 383, 1071, 1136, 1283, 1713, 1761 drop to 0\u20133 events total across the entire 15000-unit post-period (step_20). Symmetrically, the new cohort (402, 686, 879, 928, 1032, 1605, 1014, 970) was essentially non-existent before \u2014 0\u20132 events over 15000 units (step_21) \u2014 then jumps to 37\u201338 events each (step_22). The group also goes silent in [71323, 72322] (step_31), a clean seam between regimes.\n\n**Confounders ruled out.**\n- *Volume/popularity:* group event counts are flat across the period (217/189/147/149/198/205, step_06) \u2014 the partner set changes while activity does not.\n- *Graph-wide turnover:* control node 882, the single most active node (step_23), shows ordinary idiosyncratic churn with partial overlap (1074 persists) and no shared cohort (steps 25\u201326).\n- *Group specificity:* hubs 1713 and 1071 connect to *exactly* the 12 group members before the switch (steps